# Project Standards

## Pre-commit and Testing
- Always run `pre-commit` and fix any reported violations before committing code.
- Always run `pytest` to ensure all tests pass successfully before committing code.

## Documentation
- All public methods and datatypes must be documented using comprehensive docstrings.
- Docstrings must explicitly include descriptions for all input arguments and output return values (e.g. using Google style).

## Automated Testing
- Any new or updated code logic must have corresponding automated tests.
- When testing multiple scenarios, prefer using `@pytest.mark.parametrize` to achieve broad coverage with less code.
- Ensure that automated tests are not just for the happy path; they must also explicitly cover corner cases and error handling scenarios.
